From dc74870e309b159cb05f4d833d860011fc922b25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Fabio <fabio@git.it>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 14:09:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] serve webdav: add --disable-depth-infinity to stop whole tree
 listings using lots of memory (backport)

A PROPFIND with Depth: infinity, or with no Depth header, lists the
whole tree in one response. On a big tree this reads every directory
into the directory cache, using memory in proportion to the number of
files, which can run a small host out of memory.

With --disable-depth-infinity these requests are rejected with 403 and
a propfind-finite-depth error, as allowed by RFC 4918, and clients list
one level at a time with Depth: 1. The default is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 cmd/serve/webdav/webdav.go      | 37 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++------
 cmd/serve/webdav/webdav_test.go | 38 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 69 insertions(+), 6 deletions(-)

